course: dictionary
lesson: 3327
title: Evenly
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Evenly means in equal parts, so everyone gets the same amount. If 12 sweets are shared evenly between 3 friends, each friend gets 4. Nobody gets more and nobody gets less.
explain: Evenly also means smoothly and in a level way. When you spread butter evenly on toast, it covers the whole slice with no thick lumps and no bare patches. Evenly is an adverb, so it tells you how something is done: shared, spread, cut.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Jobs are not spread evenly» tells you some towns have more jobs than others, so the jobs are not in fair, equal amounts. «The 12 numbers are spread evenly» on a clock face means the gaps between the numbers are the same. Try your meaning in the sentence: equally spread still makes sense.
explain: In maths, when a number divides evenly, the share has no remainder. 12 divides evenly by 3, because 12 ÷ 3 = 4 with nothing left over. Each group gets the total divided by the number of groups.
fact: Evenly means in equal parts, so everyone gets the same.
fact: Evenly also means smoothly and in a level way, like spreading butter evenly.
fact: «Divides evenly» means a number splits into equal groups with no remainder: 12 divides evenly by 3.
fact: Each group gets the total divided by the number of groups: 12 ÷ 3 = 4.
fact: A big water lily leaf can hold a small child if the weight is spread evenly.
exercise: Mum shares 12 biscuits evenly between 3 children. How many does each child get? | *4 | 9 | 3 | 6
exercise: «The 12 numbers are spread evenly» on a clock face. What does evenly mean here? | *With equal gaps between the numbers | Very quickly | Only at the top and bottom | All crowded on the left side
exercise: Ella spreads jam on her toast. Which is the best way to spread it? | *Smoothly and evenly across the whole slice | Off the edge of the plate | Only around the edge | In one thick lump in the middle
test: Which phrase means the same as «shared evenly»? | Given away to strangers | Hidden in a box | *Given in equal parts | Given in unequal amounts
test: 12 apples are split evenly between 4 friends. How many apples does each friend get? | *3 | 2 | 16 | 8
exam: Does 15 divide evenly by 5? | No, because 5 is too small | Yes, because 5 is bigger than 3 | No, because 15 is an odd number | *Yes, 15 ÷ 5 = 3 with no remainder
